# The opposite direction, same two -e paths. `grep_error_log` already failed
# closed on an unreadable log before this scenario existed; it is here as the
# PARITY half, so the suite states both directions rather than leaving a reader
# to assume the one it does not exercise.
#
# /gone is rooted at a directory that does not exist, so nginx writes an
# [error] line naming the failed open() while serving THIS case -- a line that
# is genuinely inside the case's own offset slice, not a startup line an
# earlier case could have supplied.
name    the failed open this case provoked is visible in the error log
send    GET /gone/x HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=404
grep_error_log  No such file or directory
